  <revision rev="9" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>1c601a662d8a3a87735b0989d7b14b31</srcmd5>
    <version>0.56.0</version>
    <time>1786304677</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.56.0 (from 0.50.0). Supersedes SR 1370351, which carried the identical tree; the only change is the changelog, which now also records CVE-2025-22620 (boo#1236139) as a bug this version is not affected by (gix-worktree-state is 0.33.0, far above the 0.17.0 that fixed the world-writable checkout of executable files).

Security: this pulls in the fixes released with gitoxide 0.52.1 and gix 0.83.0, most notably CVE-2026-40034 (boo#1266434), where the CommandForbiddenInModules trust check could be bypassed in gix_submodule::File::update(), allowing arbitrary command execution from a crafted .gitmodules file. Also fixed: a submodule name validation bypass allowing traversal out of .git/modules with credential disclosure, symlinked .gitmodules being followed from outside the repository, several DoS vectors in gix-pack, and HTTP credentials leaking to a redirected host in the curl transport.

NOTE FOR LEGAL REVIEW: License changes from 'Apache-2.0 OR MIT' to '(Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND MPL-2.0'. This is a correction, not a new obligation - uluru (MPL-2.0) was already statically linked in 0.50.0, reached via gix-pack. The derivation is recorded in a Legal-Review-Notice comment above the tag, re-derived with 'cargo tree --offline -p gitoxide -e normal' over the 500-crate vendored tree (254 in the linked graph). r-efi is absent from the Linux graph. MPL-2.0 section 3.2 is satisfied because vendor.tar.zst ships in the src.rpm.

Also: require rust &gt;= 1.85 as upstream declares (edition 2024), build against pkgconfig(openssl), drop the Group tag, and follow the upstream repository move to the GitoxideLabs organisation.

Built and verified on aarch64: rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness, %check green, source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1370355</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="10" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>c7baff3907a53927cb4d6a7f148e0449</srcmd5>
    <version>0.57.0</version>
    <time>1787566246</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to gitoxide 0.57.0.

- New gix clone --revision fetches and checks out a single revision
  (full ref, HEAD or object id) with a detached HEAD; the old panic
  when a full object id was passed to with_ref_name() is fixed.
- Relative date parsing now follows git: several count/unit pairs in
  input order, spelled-out counts, optional &quot;ago&quot;, a leading &quot;@&quot;, and
  calendar month/year steps where a day past the end of the shorter
  target month rolls over.
- gix commit verify checks signatures through the library instead of
  spawning gpg, honouring the configured gpg program and trust level;
  gix revision explain no longer mislabels conflict stages.
- Vendored dependencies refreshed; jwalk replaced by dua-core (MIT).
  The License tag was re-derived over the new vendor tree and is
  unchanged: uluru (MPL-2.0) remains the only copyleft crate linked
  into the binaries.

No patches are carried. Built locally with &quot;osc build --clean
openSUSE_Tumbleweed aarch64&quot;: green, %check ok, rpmlint 0 errors /
0 warnings / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1373238</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="11" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>cc420e0af61941bfad1be7c4e8646136</srcmd5>
    <version>0.58.0</version>
    <time>1787656860</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.58.0

- gix tix now embeds the full gix-tix platform in the plumbing command,
  so standalone and plumbing invocations behave alike and amend/spill
  are reachable through gix tix
- tix decorates commits checked out by other main or linked worktrees,
  and gained -w/--worktrees to add every resolved worktree HEAD to the
  traversal tips
- gix tix no longer accepts --screen (upstream breaking change)
- Vendored dependencies refreshed; licences re-derived over the new
  vendor tree. The linked graph gains a second MPL-2.0 crate,
  option-ext, via directories/dirs-sys which gix-tix newly depends on.
  The License tag already covers MPL-2.0 and is unchanged; the
  Legal-Review-Notice above it was updated to record the derivation.</comment>
    <requestid>1373556</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
